id: pm-rl-unit-guard
title: Refuse a recursive promotion when any declared workflow unit regresses
description: Let a fixed evaluation plan bound the empirical regression of every correlation unit with one sealed declaration.
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-11-20T03:13:56.111Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-27T15:29:22.312Z"
assignee: pi-glm
claim_principal: pi-glm
author: codex-sol
acceptance_criteria: "Check all complete paired units exactly in either objective direction before promotion and preserve independent approval and resource bounds.; Preserve legacy comparisons and fail closed on incomplete, changed or sequential guarded plans.; Measure masking and equivalent-plan token savings on seeded synthetic workflows through the SDK and CLI."
parent: pm-rl-apvf
comments[22]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-20T03:14:15.851Z",codex-sol,"Ranked by value / (risk x effort), each dimension 1 to 5. Per-unit regression guard 5/(1x2)=2.50: current plan caps protected cohorts at 32 and a mean masks a single workflow loss. Learned context routing 5/(3x4)=0.42: existing public history-prefix task has 943 fit and 385 final items, but completion after choosing a projection lacks a counterfactual. Further meta-loop search 3/(3x4)=0.25: bounded recipe and proposer search already exist, with zero promotions in the published transfer replay. All three retain sealed limits, independent human approval and fail-closed lineage."
  "2026-11-20T03:14:20.756Z",codex-sol,"Implement optional max_unit_regression on fixed plans. Reuse exact decimal arithmetic on paired members within each declared correlation unit. Report one worst unit and the count in breach, keep earlier cohorts and aggregate gates effective, and retest persisted evidence and the authoritative promotion command."
  "2026-11-20T03:19:28.916Z",codex-sol,"Seed 42, 32 synthetic workflow units, 64 paired observations. Aggregate candidate 0.96875 vs incumbent 0.03125 passes. Both equivalent protections refuse the one loss of 1 on workflow-1. tiktoken 0.14.0 o200k_base over minified complete plan/report: 2086/1461 tokens using explicit cohorts, 1062/293 with the unit guard. Saving 2192 of 3547 context tokens (61.8%); inference calls zero."
  "2026-11-20T03:23:01.925Z",codex-sol,"Both new deterministic tests passed directly. The real SDK-backed CLI rejected the masked regression, kept the candidate unpromoted, and then spent the same single Decision allowance on a passing candidate. The maximum supported 10000-member plan also identified its last regressing unit. Typecheck, build, test typecheck, lint, duplicate and docstring checks passed. Changelog regeneration after fetching tags and changelog:check passed with no tracked diff. Running the package-wide coverage gate on the Node 26 PR profile, including all test files that reference the changed modules."
  "2026-11-20T03:24:17.307Z",codex-sol,Implementation commit 49453a9. The native fixed-plan promotion path accepts sealed scores. Automatic submission of an independent second benchmark by the built-in trainer is tracked separately in pm-rl-loop-panel; its existing primary score and seed-set verification remain enforced.
  "2026-11-20T03:24:53.014Z",codex-sol,The linked test command passed through pm test using snapshot workspace and no inherited pm context (exit 0). The default source workspace cannot be paired with pm-context none. The built package dry-run contains both evaluator JS and declarations and the README.
  "2026-11-20T03:27:19.354Z",codex-sol,"Commits 49453a9 and a92af33 contain the guard, tests, measured example and trainer follow-up. Exact package test inventory is 91 files. The Node 26 package coverage command is running at PR depth with all files and the original four thresholds of 100 percent. The aggregate result is pending."
  "2026-11-20T03:46:33.997Z",codex-sol,"On implementation and tracking head 90f91c9a8b84f236da460957ec1397d659700768, both required CI jobs passed. Node 22 ran all 91 files at PR depth: 1497 passed, 21 skipped, zero failed. Node 26 merged all four coverage shards across 65 authored source files: statements, branches, functions and lines each 100.00%. Release checks and CodeQL passed. The whole touched file passed locally (11/11). The separate local Node 26 coverage attempt exceeded the pre-existing 600-second vector-retry watchdog; the same test passed on hosted Node 26 in 36.46 seconds. Coverage evidence: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/actions/runs/44667912800/job/136067701193 . PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/pull/190 . Claim released in 90f91c9; tracking stays open."
  "2026-11-20T05:12:33.899Z",codex-sol,Investigate CodeRabbit thread PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs651fgQ on PR #190. Reproduce the displayed loss at large negative bounds and compute the paired difference before normalizing. Check other guard and report paths for the same cancellation.
  "2026-11-20T05:14:37.294Z",codex-sol,The new extreme-bounds regression test failed on the old arithmetic after the exact guard counted one violation. The shared unitDifferences helper now divides the raw paired difference by the finite reward span. The same test covers the protected-cohort display. Exact mean comparisons and violation counts are preserved.
  "2026-11-20T05:15:24.244Z",codex-sol,The same one-row input still reconstructs both aggregate means as 0. Follow-up pm-rl-aggregate-mean-precision tracks aggregate reconstruction and review of sequential inputs because they feed the score and inference contracts.
  "2026-11-20T05:16:43.022Z",codex-sol,CodeRabbit thread PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs651fgQ maps to commit 535394115bed90f6205b138691c7924bf64d0ecd. The paired-difference fix and regression test cover unit and protected-cohort report precision.
  "2026-11-20T05:22:16.583Z",codex-sol,The standalone evaluation-plan and worst-cohort acceptance runners reproduced the same registration and process-identity refusals on 1e518b7 and on the fix. Follow-up pm-rl-eval-acceptance-fixtures tracks their replay fixtures.
  "2026-11-20T05:27:33.801Z",codex-sol,"The whole quick worst-cohort suite passed 12 of 12. Typecheck, test build, lint and changelog checks passed. The broader direct suite and full coverage run are in progress. The controller-boundaries cleanup case passed an isolated retry using the documented local harness time scale."
  "2026-11-20T05:34:47.492Z",codex-sol,"Local gates passed: npm run typecheck, npm run build:test, npm run lint, and PM_TEST_DEPTH=quick node --test test/worst-cohort.test.ts (12 passed). npm run coverage on Node 26.13.0 hit the known 600-second test/baseline.test.ts vector-retry watchdog, so the four 100 percent thresholds need exact-head CI. The broader quick suite is still running. The standalone lifecycle, sequential, compatibility and decision-evidence replays passed. The evaluation-plan, worst-cohort and shadow scripts reproduced the same errors on 1e518b7 and are tracked in pm-rl-eval-acceptance-fixtures."
  "2026-11-27T12:57:35.435Z",pi-glm,"Inventory of what already exists on main (PR #190, commit 1b3e965, plus the arithmetic fix 5353941): evaluation-plan.ts parses optional max_unit_regression on fixed plans (sequential+guard refuses eval_plan_stopping), evaluateUnitGuard checks every complete unit with exact rational paired means, direction-aware (maximize/minimize), inclusive limits, worst-unit tie-break on the smallest label, violations count; evaluatePlan overrides the verdict with code eval_unit_regression on any breach; validateEvaluationReport guards the emitted shape; verifyEvaluationScore propagates the typed refusal at promotion; CLI rl eval plan register/show/evaluate expose it (details include max_unit_regression and unit_guard), the promote command refuses with eval_unit_regression, and the README documents the seeded seed-42 study with a tiktoken table. Tests: test/worst-cohort.test.ts per-unit guard cases, test/fixtures/unit-guard-study.ts emits the raw three-plan comparison for external token counting. Remaining gaps in this slice: (1) the eval_unit_regression refusal and report reason do not name the worst unit, its two scores or the bound, so a refused promotion does not say why in one call; unit_guard carries only the signed improvement, not both per-unit means; (2) no exhaustive decision/transition table test (guard x complete x outcome x direction x plan changed/sequential); (3) the masking/token-savings measurement is not one reproducible script: the recorded README numbers were counted externally with tiktoken and the fixture only emits raw JSON, with no CLI-side measurement; (4) the rl eval plan register/evaluate --help descriptions do not mention the per-unit guard. I will close exactly these four gaps, preserving every existing behaviour."
  "2026-11-27T13:30:47.855Z",pi-glm,"Revert proofs (behavioural revert of only the changed functions in a disposable copy, restored before any commit): (1) reverting evaluateUnitGuard/unitDifferences back to the pre-change report (no per-unit candidate/incumbent means, static refusal reason) makes 3 tests fail (per-unit guard seals, decision table, masked-workflow promotion) 0/3 pass, restored 3/3 pass. (2) reverting verifyEvaluationScore back to the generic typed refusal (no unit/scores/bound witness) makes the masked-workflow promotion test fail 0/1, restored 1/1. (3) reverting the three CLI --help descriptions makes the CLI help surface test fail 0/1, restored 1/1. Local note: npm run audit:identities exits 1 in this shared clone already on origin/main (the physical object database retains a pre-rewrite historical identity; CI audits fresh checkouts and passes), so that gate is compared, not introduced, by this branch."
  "2026-11-27T14:04:03.281Z",pi-glm,"Design of this slice (all four gaps closed, no existing behaviour weakened): (1) unit_guard now carries the worst unit's displayed candidate_mean and incumbent_mean alongside the existing improvement/bound/violations (exact rational decision arithmetic unchanged; validateEvaluationReport bounds both new means inside reward_bounds); (2) the eval_unit_regression verdict reason and the typed promotion refusal name the unit, both scores, the bound, the violation count and the shared sealed-design remedy, so one promote call states the cause (the SDK error-context contract is strictly typed, so the witness text lives in the message and context.why); (3) test/worst-cohort.test.ts gains the required transition/decision table (guard present/absent x complete/incomplete x improved/equal/regressed x maximize/minimize, plus changed-digest drift, sequential-with-guard refusal and preserved sequential-without-guard) and a CLI help-surface test; (4) test/unit-guard-measure.ts is the one-command reproducible measurement: build, npm pack, install the exact archive into a fresh non-git scratch tracker, replay the seeded 42 study through the SDK and the real pm CLI (JSON and TOON) in both directions, and count o200k_base tokens with the new pinned devDependency js-tiktoken 1.0.21. Local gates: typecheck, build, build:test, lint, duplicates (0 clones), docstring (66 files, 592 declarations) pass; npm run audit:identities fails identically on origin/main in this shared clone (pre-existing local object-database condition, CI passes on fresh checkouts). PM_TEST_DEPTH=quick across all 19 test files that import the touched modules: 349 passed, 1 skipped, 0 failed."
  "2026-11-27T14:17:24.074Z",pi-glm,"Implementation commit 5ed4186 on branch feat/unit-regression-promotion-guard, PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/pull/213 (slice scoped to the four inventory gaps; the guard core from PR #190 is unchanged). Reproducible measurement via node test/unit-guard-measure.ts: masking confirmed through SDK and CLI in both directions (aggregate 0.96875 vs 0.03125 promotes; workflow-1 refuses with candidate mean 0 / incumbent mean 1 / bound 0 in maximize and the mirrored scores in minimize; the equivalent 32-cohort plan refuses too); equivalent-plan savings 2,163 of 3,546 tokens (61.0 percent) with the pinned js-tiktoken o200k_base counts; the 86-token compact refusal replaces reading the 2,214-token raw plan plus observations (96.1 percent saved); the three refusals precede the single approved promotion, which the one passing candidate consumes. Exact-head CI carries the full coverage gate at unchanged 100 percent thresholds; pending run URLs will be added here if CI is still running at the cutoff."
  "2026-11-27T15:23:36.389Z",pi-glm,"Re-review round 1, blocking finding fixed (class closed, not the line). Rule violated: displayed diagnostic means must be correctly rounded exact sums, never running float averages that cancel. Instances found and fixed: (1) the per-unit guard's candidate_mean, incumbent_mean and improvement and (2) the protected-cohort improvement both ran incremental float averages (evaluateUnitGuard/evaluateCohorts over unitDifferences); both now derive from exact rational per-unit sums through a new roundRationalMean wrapper that pre-scales decimals into subnormal units before the sealed roundFloatMean core, so the reviewer's case (candidate [1e16, 0, -1e16] vs incumbent [1e16, 1, -1e16]) reports candidate mean 0, incumbent mean 0.3333333333333333, improvement -0.3333333333333333 instead of three zeros. (3) validateEvaluationReport's improvement domain compared against the float subtraction hi - lo, which is one ulp TIGHTER than the exact reward width (0.3 - 0.1 = 0.19999999999999998 vs the exact 0.2), falsely refusing legitimate correctly rounded values; the bound is now the correctly rounded exact width (monotone rounding keeps every produced improvement inside it). Searched the package for other instances: the aggregate top-level candidate_mean/incumbent_mean reconstruction and the sequential boundary means are decision-bearing sealed legacy comparisons, deliberately unchanged here (preserve legacy comparisons) and already tracked by pm-rl-aggregate-mean-precision from the previous round. New tests: the reviewer's adversarial case in both directions plus a seeded property loop (4-member units, even-integer rows below 2^15 magnitude and a small offset loss, BigInt-sum oracle, exact /4 dyadic means) covering the guard and cohort report paths. Revert proof: with the pre-fix product code the two new tests fail 0/2 (improvement trial 0 assertion plus the adversarial case); with the fix restored they pass 2/2 and the whole worst-cohort quick file passes 16/16."
  "2026-11-27T15:29:13.248Z",pi-glm,"Re-review non-blocking finding 1 fixed: the token benchmark now counts the plans exactly as sealed for the replay (the candidate-overridden declarations registered with the CLI), not the lookalike fixture plans. The sealed rl-guarded plan counts 1,061 tokens as the reviewer measured; the recorded output and README table are updated (aggregate-only 1,053/216, per-unit-guard 1,061/323, 32-protected-cohorts 2,084/1,462; equivalent-plan savings 2,162 of 3,546, 61.0 percent; the 86-token compact refusal replaces reading the 2,215-token sealed plan plus observations, 96.1 percent saved). Rule: measure the artifact actually sealed and replayed; every token count in the script (equivalent plans and the raw refusal comparison) now reads the sealed objects."
  "2026-11-27T15:29:22.312Z",pi-glm,"Re-review non-blocking finding 2 fixed: the rl generation promote help no longer implies a sealed evaluation verdict is always required. The description now reads 'Promote a candidate generation after contamination and budget checks pass; a sealed evaluation plan, when registered, is enforced with its per-unit regression guard.' and the promoteGeneration docstring matches. Rule: help text must state optional enforcement as conditional; searched all command descriptions and docstrings touched by this slice, the register and evaluate descriptions already state the optional guard accurately. The help-surface test now asserts the conditional wording and rejects the old overstatement."
